The strongest reusable idea is an evaluation rubric for agent shells aimed at non-professional operators: stable default workflow, visible actions, low context overhead, memory that survives restarts, and recovery paths that do not require the user to become a developer.', 'Immediate interpretation', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-source-note', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-source-note#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-source-note#5', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-source-note', 5, 'Verification needs',
  '## Verification needs

- Identify which exact OpenClaw/OpenClow/Crab implementation the speaker uses.
- Check Hermes claims against NousResearch Hermes docs/repo.
- Check Codex CLI/runtime claims against official OpenAI docs/repo.
- Compare with a few community reports from non-professional or semi-professional users.
- Security-review Telegram/CRM/business-agent recommendations before any standard.', 'a24d221296724d3d222bbe582a44cc2d5211ecf1899806da5ff76007db9187fe', 65
);
