- OpenAI''s prompt-injection article emphasizes that dangerous actions or sensitive transmissions should not happen silently, and recommends controls similar to what a human agent would need.
- OWASP lists prompt injection as a top LLM application risk and includes broader GenAI security guidance.
- Anthropic computer-use docs warn that model-controlled environments should be sandboxed, kept away from sensitive data, domain-limited and confirmed by humans for meaningful real-world consequences.', 'Verification against current sources', '2026-05-26-openclaw-hacked-prompt-injection-source-note', '2026-05-26-openclaw-hacked-prompt-injection-source-note#6');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-26-openclaw-hacked-prompt-injection-source-note#7', '2026-05-26-openclaw-hacked-prompt-injection-source-note', 7, 'Source-quality notes',
  '## Source-quality notes

- Strong: live adversarial demo plus official OpenAI, Anthropic and OWASP docs.
- Moderate: claims about Claude Opus 4.6 behavior in this exact scenario; the video is a single demo, not a benchmark.
- Weak: popularity/authority claims about specific people/tools; useful for context, not for standards.', 'ab38c22f582c09b4abc58454b4c14813a668771da2ad56e134e01daaff8bf42d', 67
);
