Refinement status: codex-refined', 'Signal: OpenAI realtime audio models for voice agents', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#2', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', 2, 'Core signal',
  '## Core signal

- OpenAI announced three realtime audio models for the API on 2026-05-07: `GPT-Realtime-2`, `GPT-Realtime-Translate` and `GPT-Realtime-Whisper`.
- The strongest agent-engineering signal is not "better voice" in general; it is the shift toward voice agents that can stay in a conversation while reasoning, calling tools and updating the user about background work.
- Voice-agent UX needs explicit preambles and action transparency: when a tool call or reasoning step takes time, the agent should say what it is doing instead of going silent.
- `GPT-Realtime-Translate` makes multilingual voice-to-voice workflows more practical for support, education, events and media, especially when speakers switch language or use technical terms.
- `GPT-Realtime-Whisper` makes live speech usable as workflow input: captions, meeting notes, support summaries, agent memory capture and real-time follow-up actions.
- The official source frames three product patterns worth tracking for Techscope: voice-to-action, systems-to-voice and voice-to-voice.', 'f8ba78b097cddd97760d130f13c389ffaab02333262029e8b183dddc8d8ebb73', 195
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Core signal

- OpenAI announced three realtime audio models for the API on 2026-05-07: `GPT-Realtime-2`, `GPT-Realtime-Translate` and `GPT-Realtime-Whisper`.
- The strongest agent-engineering signal is not "better voice" in general; it is the shift toward voice agents that can stay in a conversation while reasoning, calling tools and updating the user about background work.
- Voice-agent UX needs explicit preambles and action transparency: when a tool call or reasoning step takes time, the agent should say what it is doing instead of going silent.
- `GPT-Realtime-Translate` makes multilingual voice-to-voice workflows more practical for support, education, events and media, especially when speakers switch language or use technical terms.
- `GPT-Realtime-Whisper` makes live speech usable as workflow input: captions, meeting notes, support summaries, agent memory capture and real-time follow-up actions.
- The official source frames three product patterns worth tracking for Techscope: voice-to-action, systems-to-voice and voice-to-voice.', 'Core signal', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#3', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', 3, 'Technical details',
  '## Technical details

- The video demo shows `GPT-Realtime-Translate` translating live speech and handling language switches and technical terms.
- The `GPT-Realtime-2` demo shows a voice assistant reading calendar context, staying quiet until a trigger phrase, acknowledging background work and updating a CRM with meeting context.
- The official article states that `GPT-Realtime-2` supports preambles, parallel tool calls, stronger recovery behavior, longer context for agentic workflows, domain terminology retention, controllable tone and adjustable reasoning effort.
- The official article states that `GPT-Realtime-Translate` supports 70+ input languages and 13 output languages.
- The official article states that `GPT-Realtime-Whisper` is a streaming speech-to-text model for low-latency live transcription.
- Pricing and model availability are current as of the official 2026-05-07 OpenAI article and must be rechecked before implementation.', 'ca4074e1af08560f8c6943c28f114e1528ff6d2eb075e80b8dbbb5b707654667', 171
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Technical details

- The video demo shows `GPT-Realtime-Translate` translating live speech and handling language switches and technical terms.
- The `GPT-Realtime-2` demo shows a voice assistant reading calendar context, staying quiet until a trigger phrase, acknowledging background work and updating a CRM with meeting context.
- The official article states that `GPT-Realtime-2` supports preambles, parallel tool calls, stronger recovery behavior, longer context for agentic workflows, domain terminology retention, controllable tone and adjustable reasoning effort.
- The official article states that `GPT-Realtime-Translate` supports 70+ input languages and 13 output languages.
- The official article states that `GPT-Realtime-Whisper` is a streaming speech-to-text model for low-latency live transcription.
- Pricing and model availability are current as of the official 2026-05-07 OpenAI article and must be rechecked before implementation.', 'Technical details', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#4', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', 4, 'Agent design implications',
  '## Agent design implications

- Future voice agents need an "audible tool-use contract": preambles, progress updates, recovery phrases and clear handoff when actions are delayed.
- Voice interfaces should treat silence as a failure mode. If reasoning/tool calls take time, the agent needs a user-facing status strategy.
- Realtime transcription can become an intake channel for Techscope: meetings, voice notes and spoken Telegram/audio messages could become source artifacts before signal extraction.
- Voice-to-action agents need stricter privacy and confirmation rules than text agents because they may act on calendar, CRM, dashboard or connected-device context.
- Multilingual voice support may become useful for customer support agents and education tools, but quality must be evaluated per language/domain.', '20f245612d01697d748a098f5dff13114022a37f3b71d9a75965d1864b555a3b', 156
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Agent design implications

- Future voice agents need an "audible tool-use contract": preambles, progress updates, recovery phrases and clear handoff when actions are delayed.
- Voice interfaces should treat silence as a failure mode. If reasoning/tool calls take time, the agent needs a user-facing status strategy.
- Realtime transcription can become an intake channel for Techscope: meetings, voice notes and spoken Telegram/audio messages could become source artifacts before signal extraction.
- Voice-to-action agents need stricter privacy and confirmation rules than text agents because they may act on calendar, CRM, dashboard or connected-device context.
- Multilingual voice support may become useful for customer support agents and education tools, but quality must be evaluated per language/domain.', 'Agent design implications', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#5', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', 5, 'Candidate rules',
  '## Candidate rules

- For voice agents, require preambles or progress updates for slow reasoning/tool calls.
- Do not let voice agents perform destructive or sensitive actions without confirmation.
- Treat live transcript as raw/source material; index only source notes, signals, briefs and reviews.
- Before adopting realtime audio models, verify model IDs, pricing, data residency, retention/privacy terms and supported regions in official docs.
- Add evals for interruption handling, trigger phrases, silence/recovery behavior, multilingual terms and tool-call transparency.', '05b793ae134d2dcae01b058ed309f9c108e366ea400cf09b9b7e5d4dc776a1ff', 107
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Candidate rules

- For voice agents, require preambles or progress updates for slow reasoning/tool calls.
- Do not let voice agents perform destructive or sensitive actions without confirmation.
- Treat live transcript as raw/source material; index only source notes, signals, briefs and reviews.
- Before adopting realtime audio models, verify model IDs, pricing, data residency, retention/privacy terms and supported regions in official docs.
- Add evals for interruption handling, trigger phrases, silence/recovery behavior, multilingual terms and tool-call transparency.', 'Candidate rules', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal#6', '2026-05-16-youtube-transcript-we-re-introducing-three-audio-models-in-the-api-signal', 6, 'Noise removed',
  '## Noise removed

- Removed demo banter, repeated sales phrasing and transcript-only timestamps.
- Removed CRM demo details except where they illustrate tool-use and progress-update behavior.
