- Preserve cross-review for high-blast-radius work, but avoid turning every small task into a multi-agent ceremony.', 'Agent design implications', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-12-харнесы-умирают-часть-2-signal', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-12-харнесы-умирают-часть-2-signal#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-12-харнесы-умирают-часть-2-signal#5', '2026-05-17-2026-05-17-telegram-telegram-user-12-харнесы-умирают-часть-2-signal', 5, 'Candidate rules',
  '## Candidate rules

- Build harnesses from repeated pain, not from architectural enthusiasm.
- A harness should save time on planning, debugging, tracking or verification; otherwise remove it.
- Keep memory/process/tool access; prune ceremony.
- For large codebase changes, cross-model or second-session review can be worth the cost.', '2a11c998a076b2a06aea4e7a2e5417d3ad7e2f1e179cfc972553c2d55f9b2450', 65
);
