INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief#2', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief', 2, 'Summary',
  '## Summary

Статья Битрикс24 описывает восемь практических проблем MCP-server development. Главный вывод для Techscope: MCP server нельзя проектировать как обычную API-обертку. MCP tool surface является интерфейсом для недетерминированной модели, поэтому инструменты должны быть сценарными, самодостаточными, семантически ясными, безопасными, тестируемыми через model behavior and bounded by context limits.', 'f2f4e335154bb34375f2c1710281738e5f7b5996e2ab41fe76be6b42b78ee3db', 64
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Summary

Статья Битрикс24 описывает восемь практических проблем MCP-server development. Главный вывод для Techscope: MCP server нельзя проектировать как обычную API-обертку. MCP tool surface является интерфейсом для недетерминированной модели, поэтому инструменты должны быть сценарными, самодостаточными, семантически ясными, безопасными, тестируемыми через model behavior and bounded by context limits.', 'Summary', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief#3', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief', 3, 'Key claims',
  '## Key claims

- Авторизация в MCP clients пока неоднородна; remote MCP auth требует client compatibility matrix.
- 1:1 mapping API endpoints to MCP tools creates tool-selection confusion.
- Long dependent chains are brittle; prefer high-level tools that hide IDs and sequencing.
- Tool descriptions and parameter descriptions are the only UI the model reliably sees.
- Error messages should be written as recovery prompts.
- Unit tests test tool code, not whether the model uses tools correctly; add scenario evals and smoke tests.
- Prompt injection can enter through user prompts, database/API content and malicious MCP server outputs.
- Tool responses must be bounded and paginated to preserve context.', 'd4aa7bda471c37d971c16a4103d70b82678e15730a0af29023eef15c4b2717b7', 149
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Key claims

- Авторизация в MCP clients пока неоднородна; remote MCP auth требует client compatibility matrix.
- 1:1 mapping API endpoints to MCP tools creates tool-selection confusion.
- Long dependent chains are brittle; prefer high-level tools that hide IDs and sequencing.
- Tool descriptions and parameter descriptions are the only UI the model reliably sees.
- Error messages should be written as recovery prompts.
- Unit tests test tool code, not whether the model uses tools correctly; add scenario evals and smoke tests.
- Prompt injection can enter through user prompts, database/API content and malicious MCP server outputs.
- Tool responses must be bounded and paginated to preserve context.', 'Key claims', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief#4', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief', 4, 'Techscope implications',
  '## Techscope implications

- Create `mcp-tool-design` standard before building real MCP servers.
- Prefer local-first MCP servers until auth/client support is clear.
- Keep tool count small: start with 3-5 scenario tools per server.
- Add eval fixtures for expected tool choice and parameter shape.
- Treat error text as part of prompt engineering.
- Require least privilege, audit logs and confirmation for destructive actions.
- Add response-size policy: default limits, pagination and summarization.', '6734b6833fc9c67a51dae2f070deacf375725826553325d24671a17aaafe79fc', 100
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Techscope implications

- Create `mcp-tool-design` standard before building real MCP servers.
- Prefer local-first MCP servers until auth/client support is clear.
- Keep tool count small: start with 3-5 scenario tools per server.
- Add eval fixtures for expected tool choice and parameter shape.
- Treat error text as part of prompt engineering.
- Require least privilege, audit logs and confirmation for destructive actions.
- Add response-size policy: default limits, pagination and summarization.', 'Techscope implications', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief#5', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief', 5, 'Relationship to harness engineering',
  '## Relationship to harness engineering

This article complements OpenAI harness engineering:

- Harness engineering says prompts, skills, tests, lints and review agents are guardrails.
- MCP pitfall analysis says MCP tool schema, descriptions, errors and response shapes are also guardrails.
- Together they imply: agent tools must be designed, tested and documented as part of the harness, not as incidental API wrappers.', '138f554499a82173d2ec6de0b4648db3e3bdda434380451d084e2861fc5d80ea', 84
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Relationship to harness engineering

This article complements OpenAI harness engineering:

- Harness engineering says prompts, skills, tests, lints and review agents are guardrails.
- MCP pitfall analysis says MCP tool schema, descriptions, errors and response shapes are also guardrails.
- Together they imply: agent tools must be designed, tested and documented as part of the harness, not as incidental API wrappers.', 'Relationship to harness engineering', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief', '2026-05-15-mcp-server-pitfalls-brief#5');

