INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief#2', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief', 2, 'Summary',
  '## Summary

Codbash is a local browser dashboard for managing AI coding-agent sessions across Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, OpenCode, Kiro, Kilo and Copilot Chat. The Telegram update and screenshots show the product moving from passive session browsing toward a project launcher: projects, default agent selection, new/last session controls, GitHub repo onboarding, grouped history and cost/session analytics.

For Techscope, this is interesting because agent work quickly becomes multi-session and multi-runtime. We need observability, resumption and cost visibility before running many parallel agents seriously.', '8a95c4b10f9080cc9315069324bf841e050636b360f96e7a277f42f0b41241b9', 113
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Summary

Codbash is a local browser dashboard for managing AI coding-agent sessions across Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, OpenCode, Kiro, Kilo and Copilot Chat. The Telegram update and screenshots show the product moving from passive session browsing toward a project launcher: projects, default agent selection, new/last session controls, GitHub repo onboarding, grouped history and cost/session analytics.

For Techscope, this is interesting because agent work quickly becomes multi-session and multi-runtime. We need observability, resumption and cost visibility before running many parallel agents seriously.', 'Summary', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief#3', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief', 3, 'Key claims',
  '## Key claims

- Coding-agent tools need a session cockpit, not only terminal windows.
- Project-level grouping is the right unit: sessions, costs, default agent and GitHub repo relation should attach to a project.
- Cross-agent support matters because Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, OpenCode and Kiro store sessions differently.
- `New` vs `Last` is a practical UX primitive for repeated agent work.
- Local-first dashboards are preferable for private coding sessions; SaaS observability requires stronger trust and privacy review.', '6111ba7f01e4f97b767a4888f925df446d875db346ed074c769a896c6330e506', 108
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Key claims

- Coding-agent tools need a session cockpit, not only terminal windows.
- Project-level grouping is the right unit: sessions, costs, default agent and GitHub repo relation should attach to a project.
- Cross-agent support matters because Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, OpenCode and Kiro store sessions differently.
- `New` vs `Last` is a practical UX primitive for repeated agent work.
- Local-first dashboards are preferable for private coding sessions; SaaS observability requires stronger trust and privacy review.', 'Key claims', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief#4', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief', 4, 'Evidence',
  '## Evidence

- GitHub README confirms supported agents, local browser dashboard, search/replay/resume, cost analytics, cross-agent conversion and handoff.
- Telegram screenshots show Projects, project settings, GitHub repo onboarding, contributor repos and History cost/message counts.
- GitHub API observed 2026-05-17 shows active project state: latest push 2026-05-16, 210 stars, 38 forks.', '99472625307622fcf132095105d04262f700825304d21170f4d66ffc50b36394', 68
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Evidence

- GitHub README confirms supported agents, local browser dashboard, search/replay/resume, cost analytics, cross-agent conversion and handoff.
- Telegram screenshots show Projects, project settings, GitHub repo onboarding, contributor repos and History cost/message counts.
- GitHub API observed 2026-05-17 shows active project state: latest push 2026-05-16, 210 stars, 38 forks.', 'Evidence', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief#5', '2026-05-17-codbash-agent-session-browser-brief', 5, 'Risks and caveats',
  '## Risks and caveats

- Session dashboards touch sensitive local agent logs and project paths.
- Cost analytics depend on accurate parsing of each agent''s session format.
- Launching agents from a dashboard increases the blast radius if defaults or project paths are wrong.
- Codbash should be tested locally before it influences a Techscope standard.', '220ee53ca65e3611f85cfb573cece98202e8b4c649e2b2ebeb5dc8438bc13c6f', 76
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Risks and caveats

- Session dashboards touch sensitive local agent logs and project paths.
- Cost analytics depend on accurate parsing of each agent''s session format.
