Status: draft', 'Brief: OpenClaw, Hermes and Codex CLI through advanced-user experience', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#2', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 2, 'Summary',
  '## Summary

Видео полезно как UX-свидетельство продвинутого пользователя, который не является профессиональным разработчиком, но активно использует агентские системы. Его главный практический вывод: выбор агентской среды для реальной работы определяется не "самым умным" ответом, а стабильностью контура, управлением памятью, стоимостью контекста, прозрачностью tools/skills and recovery after restart.

Для Techscope это подтверждает уже выбранную архитектуру: входящие материалы должны превращаться не в сырые длинные контексты, а в source note, refined signal, brief/review and generated wiki layer. Для будущих агентов особенно важны thin interfaces for users and explicit harness rules for memory, tools, permissions and completion.', '433a3a85058bca5c30286e3dee9719b51c3deae0729097de88251ffbca5493c9', 125
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Summary

Видео полезно как UX-свидетельство продвинутого пользователя, который не является профессиональным разработчиком, но активно использует агентские системы. Его главный практический вывод: выбор агентской среды для реальной работы определяется не "самым умным" ответом, а стабильностью контура, управлением памятью, стоимостью контекста, прозрачностью tools/skills and recovery after restart.

Для Techscope это подтверждает уже выбранную архитектуру: входящие материалы должны превращаться не в сырые длинные контексты, а в source note, refined signal, brief/review and generated wiki layer. Для будущих агентов особенно важны thin interfaces for users and explicit harness rules for memory, tools, permissions and completion.', 'Summary', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#3', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 3, 'Key claims',
  '## Key claims

- Agent shells differ mainly by harness thickness: how much context, tools, persona and memory they inject before the model answers.
- Rich/personal shells can be pleasant for individual use, but may accumulate context and become costly or unstable under heavy customization.
- Hermes-like self-improving skill workflows are attractive for business/autonomous tasks, but the claim must be verified against official Hermes docs and observed behavior.
- Codex CLI-like setups are attractive for long coding/heavy local tasks because the runtime is leaner and source-controlled workflows are easier to inspect.
- For non-coders, a useful agent must accept ordinary requests through Telegram or another familiar UI and hide command-line repair work.
- File-backed Markdown wiki memory is a strong pattern, but generated wiki pages must not override curated source artifacts.', 'eb9c03e0e2cfbb73fbd8a96d0fc63f5f3f4da526ec2ed20f5fe07d374fcff2e5', 177
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Key claims

- Agent shells differ mainly by harness thickness: how much context, tools, persona and memory they inject before the model answers.
- Rich/personal shells can be pleasant for individual use, but may accumulate context and become costly or unstable under heavy customization.
- Hermes-like self-improving skill workflows are attractive for business/autonomous tasks, but the claim must be verified against official Hermes docs and observed behavior.
- Codex CLI-like setups are attractive for long coding/heavy local tasks because the runtime is leaner and source-controlled workflows are easier to inspect.
- For non-coders, a useful agent must accept ordinary requests through Telegram or another familiar UI and hide command-line repair work.
- File-backed Markdown wiki memory is a strong pattern, but generated wiki pages must not override curated source artifacts.', 'Key claims', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#4', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 4, 'Evidence',
  '## Evidence

- Video source: ALEKSEI ULIANOV, published 2026-04-28, transcribed locally with `mlx-whisper`.
- Karpathy LLM Wiki gist, 2026-04-04, describes raw sources, generated wiki and schema as separate layers, with index/log operations.
- NousResearch `hermes-agent` repo describes skill learning, multi-provider support, gateways, memory/search and subagent delegation.
- Hermes Codex runtime docs say Codex app-server integration is opt-in and that some Hermes loop tools such as delegate_task/memory/session_search/todo are not available in stateless Codex runtime mode.
- OpenAI Codex repo/docs position Codex CLI as a local coding agent; OpenAI Codex app article frames app/CLI/IDE/cloud as related but distinct surfaces.
- arXiv memory survey frames agent memory as a write-manage-read loop and highlights privacy governance, contradiction handling and latency budgets.
- Community reports found during web check broadly match the "thin wrapper vs heavy shell" tension: some users prefer Codex as the core agent with a small messaging wrapper, while some Hermes/OpenClaw switchers report mixed results around setup, bloat and token usage.', 'c790569f12b7f3907935f6df9eb37873302df513ed9b4005e8b6841e37c53919', 215
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Evidence

- Video source: ALEKSEI ULIANOV, published 2026-04-28, transcribed locally with `mlx-whisper`.
- Karpathy LLM Wiki gist, 2026-04-04, describes raw sources, generated wiki and schema as separate layers, with index/log operations.
- NousResearch `hermes-agent` repo describes skill learning, multi-provider support, gateways, memory/search and subagent delegation.
- Hermes Codex runtime docs say Codex app-server integration is opt-in and that some Hermes loop tools such as delegate_task/memory/session_search/todo are not available in stateless Codex runtime mode.
- OpenAI Codex repo/docs position Codex CLI as a local coding agent; OpenAI Codex app article frames app/CLI/IDE/cloud as related but distinct surfaces.
- arXiv memory survey frames agent memory as a write-manage-read loop and highlights privacy governance, contradiction handling and latency budgets.
- Community reports found during web check broadly match the "thin wrapper vs heavy shell" tension: some users prefer Codex as the core agent with a small messaging wrapper, while some Hermes/OpenClaw switchers report mixed results around setup, bloat and token usage.', 'Evidence', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief#5', '2026-05-17-openclaw-hermes-codex-cli-advanced-user-brief', 5, 'Risks and caveats',
  '## Risks and caveats

- The source is subjective and streamer-style. It is useful signal, not proof.
- Exact "OpenClaw/OpenClow/Crab" identity is unclear and must be pinned before project-specific conclusions.
- Some web sources around OpenClaw/Hermes look promotional or inconsistent; prefer official repo/docs and dated community reports.
- Self-improving skills and auto-written wiki memory increase stale-memory, prompt-injection and accidental-permission risks.
- Business/CRM agent recommendations need separate privacy/security review before implementation.', '313ef24800f44fb30efdd87c25b7f43eabb8223037199e143eada57664032b3f', 95
);
