Date: 2026-05-17
Source: YouTube transcript plus primary-source checks
Status: draft', 'Brief: Skills vs MCP for agent tooling', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#1');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#2', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', 2, 'Summary',
  '## Summary

The useful conclusion is not "Skills killed MCP". Skills and MCP solve adjacent but different problems. MCP is a protocol for exposing external context, tools and services to agents. Skills are portable, progressive-disclosure instructions that tell an agent how to perform a task, often by using local scripts, CLIs, reference files or MCP tools. For Techscope and future coding agents, the practical rule should be: prefer skills for local repeatable workflows and process knowledge; prefer MCP for service integration, OAuth, shared governance, caching, remote/API-agent environments and standardized tool access.', '25774b9285561c822b6f7d16a0561828335219fb25ebaf3966e6fbadcb87be0c', 123
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Summary

The useful conclusion is not "Skills killed MCP". Skills and MCP solve adjacent but different problems. MCP is a protocol for exposing external context, tools and services to agents. Skills are portable, progressive-disclosure instructions that tell an agent how to perform a task, often by using local scripts, CLIs, reference files or MCP tools. For Techscope and future coding agents, the practical rule should be: prefer skills for local repeatable workflows and process knowledge; prefer MCP for service integration, OAuth, shared governance, caching, remote/API-agent environments and standardized tool access.', 'Summary', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#3', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', 3, 'Key claims',
  '## Key claims

- Skills are a better fit for workflow instructions, local scripts, local CLI wrappers, browser automation through scripts, document/file workflows and project-specific operating procedures.
- MCP is a better fit when the agent needs a standardized service boundary, OAuth/refresh-token handling, shared integration logic, centralized updates, caching/rate-limit handling, auditing or non-local/API execution.
- Context overhead is still a concern, but no longer the only argument: modern clients can lazy-load or search tools on demand.
- Skills and MCP can be layered: MCP gives access to an external system; a skill tells the agent when and how to use that access.
- Both Skills and MCP are security-sensitive. Skills can bundle executable scripts; MCP tools can expose data and arbitrary operations. Both need trust, review and sandboxing/approval policies.', 'dd30a13ee15a4e1b7129da9f516f7452e25345b8cdc1957e8e7b07f9a872d939', 175
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Key claims

- Skills are a better fit for workflow instructions, local scripts, local CLI wrappers, browser automation through scripts, document/file workflows and project-specific operating procedures.
- MCP is a better fit when the agent needs a standardized service boundary, OAuth/refresh-token handling, shared integration logic, centralized updates, caching/rate-limit handling, auditing or non-local/API execution.
- Context overhead is still a concern, but no longer the only argument: modern clients can lazy-load or search tools on demand.
- Skills and MCP can be layered: MCP gives access to an external system; a skill tells the agent when and how to use that access.
- Both Skills and MCP are security-sensitive. Skills can bundle executable scripts; MCP tools can expose data and arbitrary operations. Both need trust, review and sandboxing/approval policies.', 'Key claims', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#4', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', 4, 'Evidence',
  '## Evidence

- Agent Skills docs define the folder/`SKILL.md` model and progressive disclosure.
- OpenAI maintains a Codex skills catalog and ships system skills in Codex.
- OpenAI also hosts a public Docs MCP server and explicitly suggests pairing it with a skill, which supports the "complement, not replacement" model.
- MCP specification defines resources, prompts and tools as server features, using JSON-RPC and capability negotiation.
- OpenAI Shell docs reinforce that local command execution is powerful but needs sandboxing, allowlists/denylists and logging.
- The video transcript provides a practical migration recipe: list MCPs, find CLI/script alternatives, wrap repeatable workflows into skills, test, then remove only the MCPs that are actually redundant.', '8014f7f806f6c3118874f72c1b1443595453172411f59832731977090953c43d', 152
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Evidence

- Agent Skills docs define the folder/`SKILL.md` model and progressive disclosure.
- OpenAI maintains a Codex skills catalog and ships system skills in Codex.
- OpenAI also hosts a public Docs MCP server and explicitly suggests pairing it with a skill, which supports the "complement, not replacement" model.
- MCP specification defines resources, prompts and tools as server features, using JSON-RPC and capability negotiation.
- OpenAI Shell docs reinforce that local command execution is powerful but needs sandboxing, allowlists/denylists and logging.
- The video transcript provides a practical migration recipe: list MCPs, find CLI/script alternatives, wrap repeatable workflows into skills, test, then remove only the MCPs that are actually redundant.', 'Evidence', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#5', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', 5, 'Risks and caveats',
  '## Risks and caveats

- A skill can silently become a supply-chain risk if it bundles scripts from an untrusted source.
- MCP servers can also be risky: tool descriptions, data access and command execution need consent and authorization.
- Skills are not guaranteed to trigger unless their metadata/description is good.
- Agents can skip steps in a skill; critical workflows need checklists, assertions or executable harnesses.
- MCP token/context cost varies by client and implementation; use measurements rather than fixed assumptions.
- OAuth and shared team integrations should not be forced into skills unless a mature CLI already handles auth safely.', '78b9a2badcb81494e0c0e49a99a14b91fc31c2688a0484c6cd03d27c3bb1f7b4', 138
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Risks and caveats

- A skill can silently become a supply-chain risk if it bundles scripts from an untrusted source.
- MCP servers can also be risky: tool descriptions, data access and command execution need consent and authorization.
- Skills are not guaranteed to trigger unless their metadata/description is good.
- Agents can skip steps in a skill; critical workflows need checklists, assertions or executable harnesses.
- MCP token/context cost varies by client and implementation; use measurements rather than fixed assumptions.
- OAuth and shared team integrations should not be forced into skills unless a mature CLI already handles auth safely.', 'Risks and caveats', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#6', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', 6, 'Recommendation',
  '## Recommendation

Adopt this as a candidate standard for Techscope:

- Default to skills for repeatable local agent workflows, project conventions, command wrappers, document generation, browser scripts and internal scripts.
- Default to MCP for external service access with auth, shared team governance, server-side caching, auditability, and integrations that should be centrally maintained.
- Use skills plus MCP together when process knowledge matters: the MCP exposes the tool, the skill teaches the agent the operating procedure.
- Before adding any MCP server to a coding-agent setup, ask whether a small skill around an existing CLI/script would be cheaper, safer and easier to maintain.', 'd14fdfbb5981c74f00a6bbdd68d9e9015bc858fd3c6e4dc36fa7df9641041517', 140
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Recommendation

Adopt this as a candidate standard for Techscope:

- Default to skills for repeatable local agent workflows, project conventions, command wrappers, document generation, browser scripts and internal scripts.
- Default to MCP for external service access with auth, shared team governance, server-side caching, auditability, and integrations that should be centrally maintained.
- Use skills plus MCP together when process knowledge matters: the MCP exposes the tool, the skill teaches the agent the operating procedure.
- Before adding any MCP server to a coding-agent setup, ask whether a small skill around an existing CLI/script would be cheaper, safer and easier to maintain.', 'Recommendation', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#6');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief#7', '2026-05-17-skills-vs-mcp-agent-tooling-brief', 7, 'Next step',
  '## Next step

Create a draft standard: "agent tool integration selection: skills vs MCP vs CLI". The standard should include a decision matrix, security checklist and migration recipe.', 'beb7e691af6413dd4410ec170f881750b19e49accea1a185ec05964f4f1c76eb', 38
);
