- Config surfaces: slash commands, `config.yaml`, skills, toolsets, MCP, provider auth, gateway, local proxy.
- Portability: adapter-needed. The concept is portable; exact commands and persistence behavior are platform-specific.', 'Agent environment profile', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-autonomous-workflow-brief', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-autonomous-workflow-brief#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-autonomous-workflow-brief#5', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-autonomous-workflow-brief', 5, 'Evidence',
  '## Evidence

- Hermes official docs describe persistent `/goal`, continuation, turn budget, user message preemption, persistence and judge configuration.
- Hermes v0.14.0 release notes include `/subgoal` and goal-loop changes.
- Codex CLI 0.128.0 release notes include persisted `/goal` workflows, app-server APIs, model tools, runtime continuation and TUI controls.
- OpenAI Codex CLI docs confirm Codex CLI''s local terminal-agent model and authentication surface.
- The YouTube video demonstrates workflow usage but is secondary evidence and includes marketing content.', 'cb63d0818a1d33efbfdddc6e75e5ea6fcefa30667e82cbeda93c1b00f206f47a', 104
);
