INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief#2', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief', 2, 'Summary',
  '## Summary

Pritha creates minimal sufficient descendants, but those agents are expected to keep evolving. For Codex-native agents, the primary evolution path is opening the descendant project in Codex App and continuing work through the agent''s own instructions, manifests, tests and memory.', '89e35d6a17c8e4301f49f55d8816b3794f49feaa6b6b270e1c98286f2632ca5c', 57
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Summary

Pritha creates minimal sufficient descendants, but those agents are expected to keep evolving. For Codex-native agents, the primary evolution path is opening the descendant project in Codex App and continuing work through the agent''s own instructions, manifests, tests and memory.', 'Summary', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief#3', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief', 3, 'Key Claims',
  '## Key Claims

- A generated agent scaffold is a starting point, not a final ceiling.
- Future functionality can be added through the agent''s native interface, especially Codex App for Codex-native descendants.
- If a descendant receives an external internet resource that is not directly relevant to its mission, the agent should not silently merge it into domain memory.
- Such material should be handled as meta-improvement input: possible evidence for improving harness, memory, data handling, skills, MCP, tools, evals, UX, safety or operations.
- Useful distilled lessons can stay inside the descendant''s own memory or be sent back to Pritha/Techscope as reusable scaffold knowledge.', '7b2e9978042f2fea74a3af984fdbc694f45a048a75535419eac89c6327747375', 144
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Key Claims

- A generated agent scaffold is a starting point, not a final ceiling.
- Future functionality can be added through the agent''s native interface, especially Codex App for Codex-native descendants.
- If a descendant receives an external internet resource that is not directly relevant to its mission, the agent should not silently merge it into domain memory.
- Such material should be handled as meta-improvement input: possible evidence for improving harness, memory, data handling, skills, MCP, tools, evals, UX, safety or operations.
- Useful distilled lessons can stay inside the descendant''s own memory or be sent back to Pritha/Techscope as reusable scaffold knowledge.', 'Key Claims', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief#4', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief', 4, 'Routing Rule',
  '## Routing Rule

When an external resource arrives:

| Resource relation | Route |
| --- | --- |
| Directly supports the agent''s domain task | Process through the agent''s domain intake workflow. |
| Improves the agent''s own architecture or operations | Process as self-improvement brief/review/decision. |
| Reusable across future agents | Send distilled lesson back to Pritha/Techscope as candidate scaffold knowledge. |
| Irrelevant or weak evidence | Archive or ignore with a short note. |', '78fc4ef5448aaf06edaab275526e2dd90a1be73e7d74a864d3d836ad508edb38', 108
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Routing Rule

When an external resource arrives:

| Resource relation | Route |
| --- | --- |
| Directly supports the agent''s domain task | Process through the agent''s domain intake workflow. |
| Improves the agent''s own architecture or operations | Process as self-improvement brief/review/decision. |
| Reusable across future agents | Send distilled lesson back to Pritha/Techscope as candidate scaffold knowledge. |
| Irrelevant or weak evidence | Archive or ignore with a short note. |', 'Routing Rule', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief#5', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief', 5, 'Recommendation',
  '## Recommendation

Future Pritha descendants should document both paths: domain intake and self-improvement intake. This keeps agent memory clean while still allowing broad learning from YouTube videos, articles, repositories, docs, forum posts and other resources.', 'c7a38f1ebe4dd4f5b0c7c5329fa7154753ecd195848ff3b1bb91f2b8e2d87011', 48
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Recommendation

Future Pritha descendants should document both paths: domain intake and self-improvement intake. This keeps agent memory clean while still allowing broad learning from YouTube videos, articles, repositories, docs, forum posts and other resources.', 'Recommendation', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief', '2026-05-28-descendant-meta-improvement-input-brief#5');

