INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment#2', '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment', 2, 'One-paragraph read',
  '## One-paragraph read

This is a strong practical source for Techscope. It gives a clean routing rule for coding agents: use CLI when the task is a local, deterministic developer operation already well served by mature commands; use MCP when the agent needs a managed abstraction, rendered content, authentication, governance or auditability. It confirms our previous Skills/MCP conclusions and adds CLI as the third explicit option in the decision matrix.', 'c77b91a8a5b8717b26379d0e2b8e556d1c00fff0ae2b7d445b3ffe52670e0087', 95
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## One-paragraph read

This is a strong practical source for Techscope. It gives a clean routing rule for coding agents: use CLI when the task is a local, deterministic developer operation already well served by mature commands; use MCP when the agent needs a managed abstraction, rendered content, authentication, governance or auditability. It confirms our previous Skills/MCP conclusions and adds CLI as the third explicit option in the decision matrix.', 'One-paragraph read', '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment', '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment#3', '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment', 3, 'Why it matters',
  '## Why it matters

Techscope is building agent harnesses that will repeatedly choose between shell scripts, skills, MCP servers, browser tools and service APIs. A wrong default creates either context bloat and integration sprawl, or unsafe shell-heavy agents. This source helps us encode the choice as a reusable architecture rule.', 'e05ab6933deee177ea4cfeb8759fd0e364353fdf1b72a40d46c401e8bddfd758', 68
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Why it matters

Techscope is building agent harnesses that will repeatedly choose between shell scripts, skills, MCP servers, browser tools and service APIs. A wrong default creates either context bloat and integration sprawl, or unsafe shell-heavy agents. This source helps us encode the choice as a reusable architecture rule.', 'Why it matters', '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment', '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment#4', '2026-05-17-cli-vs-mcp-tool-selection-assessment', 4, 'Technical claims',
  '## Technical claims

- Shell commands are often more compact than MCP calls for local developer tasks.
- MCP tool schemas can create meaningful context overhead when broad servers are loaded eagerly.
- CLI tools compose naturally with pipes; MCP tool calls are more isolated.
- MCP can compress complex interactions into useful output, especially when raw CLI output is not enough.
- MCP is a better fit for service-managed auth, token refresh, per-user permissions and audit trails.
- The right answer is not CLI or MCP; it is task-dependent routing.', '5d0a34db6325c34d3c46bdd90fda364d808cecd7d72bbb29de339ad9dc2beb8f', 123
);
