INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment#2', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment', 2, 'One-paragraph read',
  '## One-paragraph read

This is genuinely useful for Techscope, but the value is not the video''s hype. The durable insight is that long-running autonomy needs a goal contract: explicit objective, acceptance criteria, independent judge, bounded continuation, pause/resume controls, subgoals, persistence, logs and post-run verification. That pattern should influence Agents Mother. Hermes itself remains an experiment candidate, not a default runtime.', 'de0d7f2d24286b6bf7ad4957b8571ea775815c3492f8a0c6ae5d48e6e59bd8e2', 81
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## One-paragraph read

This is genuinely useful for Techscope, but the value is not the video''s hype. The durable insight is that long-running autonomy needs a goal contract: explicit objective, acceptance criteria, independent judge, bounded continuation, pause/resume controls, subgoals, persistence, logs and post-run verification. That pattern should influence Agents Mother. Hermes itself remains an experiment candidate, not a default runtime.', 'One-paragraph read', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment#2');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment#3', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment', 3, 'Why it matters',
  '## Why it matters

Agents Mother is moving toward creating and operating real agents. Once agents can deploy services, run Telegram/web interfaces and perform proactive work, "just keep going" becomes dangerous. A persistent goal loop gives autonomy a harness: it tells the agent what success means, how long it may try, when it must stop and how the user can steer it.', 'bbdfe5d89d96a4a44562e61c5984f8816ae18dc2a882804563880bc9b4c02fff', 84
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Why it matters

Agents Mother is moving toward creating and operating real agents. Once agents can deploy services, run Telegram/web interfaces and perform proactive work, "just keep going" becomes dangerous. A persistent goal loop gives autonomy a harness: it tells the agent what success means, how long it may try, when it must stop and how the user can steer it.', 'Why it matters', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment#3');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment#4', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment', 4, 'Technical claims',
  '## Technical claims

- Persistent goals are stronger than prompt-only loops because the objective is stored and reused across turns.
- The judge/evaluator should be logically separate from the executor.
- Turn budget and pause/resume controls are not nice-to-have; they are required safety controls.
- Subgoals are a useful mid-run steering mechanism.
- Goals need concrete acceptance criteria, not "make it good" objectives.
- Orchestrator/worker setups such as Hermes-as-CEO / Codex-as-CTO can be useful if each worker has a scoped contract, isolated workspace and verification gate.', 'bd2e675068cef826f56541de928372ea026cc56b8cf80c8d22435877d5c106ea', 117
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Technical claims

- Persistent goals are stronger than prompt-only loops because the objective is stored and reused across turns.
- The judge/evaluator should be logically separate from the executor.
- Turn budget and pause/resume controls are not nice-to-have; they are required safety controls.
- Subgoals are a useful mid-run steering mechanism.
- Goals need concrete acceptance criteria, not "make it good" objectives.
- Orchestrator/worker setups such as Hermes-as-CEO / Codex-as-CTO can be useful if each worker has a scoped contract, isolated workspace and verification gate.', 'Technical claims', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment#4');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment#5', '2026-05-18-hermes-goal-agent-architecture-assessment', 5, 'Agent environment profile',
  '## Agent environment profile

- Agent platforms: Hermes Agent, Codex, Claude Code.
- Model context: GPT-5.5 and other OpenAI models; OpenRouter/Hermes provider routing; auxiliary judge model.
- Runtime environment: CLI, VPS/SSH, messaging gateway, Codex CLI worker, background execution.
- Config surfaces: slash commands, `config.yaml`, skills, toolsets, MCP, gateway, provider auth.
- Portability: adapter-needed.
- Codex adaptation:
  - Implement Techscope-native goal contracts in Markdown and scripts first.
  - Map `/goal` to `goal-contract + run log + evaluator report`, not to a blind always-on loop.
  - Keep source of truth in Techscope artifacts, not Hermes memory.
- Environment-specific caveats:
  - Hermes `/goal`, `/subgoal`, SessionDB persistence and gateway FIFO continuation are Hermes-specific.
  - Codex CLI `/goal` lifecycle comes from Codex CLI release behavior and may differ from Codex Desktop or this current Codex app thread.
  - Claude Code examples in the video are anecdotal unless separately verified.', 'f7d5ea80b6deb76721b6888cd17ea7f2018ad0a3ed2905a239257c11738b7c04', 195
);
