- `create_followup_checklist`

Legacy explicit CLI tool:

- `queue_codex_cli_task`, hidden unless `FESPA_ENABLE_CODEX_CLI_TOOL=true`.', 'Updated Voice-Control Boundary', '2026-05-29-fespa26-voice-control-and-feed-memory-update', '2026-05-29-fespa26-voice-control-and-feed-memory-update#5');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-29-fespa26-voice-control-and-feed-memory-update#6', '2026-05-29-fespa26-voice-control-and-feed-memory-update', 6, 'Event/Reportage Agent Pattern',
  '## Event/Reportage Agent Pattern

FESPA26 is the reference example for future event agents where the goal is not generic chat but building a curated public or internal feed.

Reusable modules:

- source intake from voice, text, links, files, media and drop inbox;
- operational memory for sources and feed items;
- stable feed card ids/numbers;
- queue jobs for media analysis, source verification, translation and card updates;
- reviewed/draft/publication states;
- explicit publication gate;
- public-site projection as a separate deploy step;
- runner status visible to the operator.

Do not reuse FESPA26 blindly for agents that do not need a feed, publication lifecycle, event source memory or media processing.', '14b7806d378214f2291fd1a88836c0321ed4ea59fb3fe76a45cf7e881ebe7257', 149
);
INSERT INTO chunks_fts (text, heading, document_id, chunk_id)
VALUES ('## Event/Reportage Agent Pattern

FESPA26 is the reference example for future event agents where the goal is not generic chat but building a curated public or internal feed.

Reusable modules:

- source intake from voice, text, links, files, media and drop inbox;
- operational memory for sources and feed items;
- stable feed card ids/numbers;
- queue jobs for media analysis, source verification, translation and card updates;
- reviewed/draft/publication states;
- explicit publication gate;
- public-site projection as a separate deploy step;
- runner status visible to the operator.

Do not reuse FESPA26 blindly for agents that do not need a feed, publication lifecycle, event source memory or media processing.', 'Event/Reportage Agent Pattern', '2026-05-29-fespa26-voice-control-and-feed-memory-update', '2026-05-29-fespa26-voice-control-and-feed-memory-update#6');

INSERT INTO chunks (id, document_id, ordinal, heading, text, hash, token_count)
VALUES (
  '2026-05-29-fespa26-voice-control-and-feed-memory-update#7', '2026-05-29-fespa26-voice-control-and-feed-memory-update', 7, 'Useful Scaffold Patterns',
  '## Useful Scaffold Patterns

- Separate live voice from durable event memory.
- Treat voice commands about product/content as feed/source tasks.
- Treat voice commands about the app itself as system-change tasks.
- Use Codex App/thread for complex operator-facing work that benefits from the current Codex context.
- Keep Codex CLI available as fallback/worker, not as the only deep-work route.
- Make fallback state explicit so the operator can see whether work is completed, pending, captured or failed.
- Preserve tool-event audit records for voice-triggered work.', '17f29db70c7e725d7296ae7f1df7e803689d30bf6c5dfdd35cc61a2caf3e72aa', 117
);
